<%# How often life emerged in each arm, every treated arm against the control at its own
    cap. It is the sweep's own outcome and decides nothing about the complexity reading. %>
<h3>How often life emerged</h3>
<div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" id="complexity-arms-emergence"
     aria-label="How often life emerged in each arm, against the control at the same cap">
  <table class="data-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Arm</th>
        <th class="numeric">Terminal runs</th>
        <th class="numeric">Emerged</th>
        <th class="numeric">Rate</th>
        <th>Control at the same cap</th>
        <th class="numeric">Against it</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% reading.arms.each do |arm| %>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <span class="mono"><%= arm.label %></span>
            <% if arm.control? %><span class="badge badge-info">control</span><% end %>
            <% if arm.barren? %><span class="badge badge-error">barren</span><% end %>
          </td>
          <td class="numeric mono"><%= arm.terminal_count %></td>
          <td class="numeric mono"><%= arm.emerged_count %></td>
          <td class="numeric mono">
            <% if arm.tested? %>
              <%= arm.emergence_fraction %> (<%= percent_value arm.emergence_rate %>)
            <% else %>
              —
            <% end %>
          </td>
          <td class="mono"><%= arm.control? ? "—" : reading.control_for(arm)&.label || "—" %></td>
          <td class="numeric mono">
            <% p_value = reading.emergence_p_value(arm) %>
            <% if p_value.nil? %>
              —
            <% else %>
              p = <%= number_with_precision(p_value, precision: 2, significant: true,
                                            strip_insignificant_zeros: true) %>
              <% if reading.emergence_significant?(arm) %>
                <span class="badge badge-warning">p &lt; 0.05</span>
              <% end %>
            <% end %>
          </td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
<p><strong><%= reading.emergence_sentence %></strong></p>
<p class="text-sm text-muted">
  One row per arm. "Terminal runs" counts the runs of the arm that reached an end with at
  least one sample, "Emerged" the confirmed crossings among them, and "Rate" the second over
  the first. "Against it" is a two-sided Fisher exact test of the arm's emerged and
  unemerged runs against those of the control at the same <span class="mono">max_tape_len</span>
  — a dash for a control itself and for an arm with nothing terminal to test. It describes
  how often life emerged and decides nothing about the complexity reading below.
</p>
